Z||000010||2birds||07-24-2000||12:07 AM||||It'll be about two weeks before I get everything together for it.  I'm caling Summitt and Ram today about the parts.  Nobody up here in the sticks can turn a flywheel, so I'm looking for a place in JAX to do it.  I have a friend with cherry-picker type engine hoist, so I'm going to try it by  taking the whole drivetrain out, then pulling the engine off the transaxle.  I did it with the engine supported by a brace last time.  PITA to line up the transaxle, and everything is over your head.<P>I'll keep you posted. <P>TCCOA.com has a good tech site, called Articles.  It's real well organized.  I don't know jack squat about websites, but it looks good to me.<p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
